<title>SLOVAKIA: BIATHLON-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP WOMEN'S 7.5 KM RELAY.</title>
<headline>BIATHLON-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP WOMEN'S 7.5 KM RELAY.</headline>
<dateline>OSRBLIE, Slovakia 1997-02-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading results of the</p>
<p>women's 7.5-km relay event at the World Biathlon Championship</p>
<p>on Saturday:</p>
<p>1. Germany (Uschi Disl, Simone Greiner-Petter-Memm, Katrin</p>
<p>    Apel, Petra Behle)	1 hour 28 minutes 36.9 seconds</p>
<p>2. Norway (Ann Elen Skjelbreid, Annette Sikveland, Liv Grete</p>
<p>    Skjelbreid, Gunn Margit Andreassen)    1:30:06.7</p>
<p>3. Russia (Olga Melnik, Galina Koukleva, Nadezhda Talanova,</p>
<p>    Olga Romasko)				  1:30:09.7</p>
<p>4. France (Christelle Gros, Delphyne Heymann-Burlet, Anne</p>
<p>    Briand, Corinne Niogret)		   1:31:19.2</p>
<p>5. Ukraine (Olena Zubrilova, Olena Petrova, Tatiana</p>
<p>    Vodopianova, Valentina Tserbe)	   1:31:58.1</p>
<p>6. Kazakhstan (Inna Sheshkel, Margarita Doulova, Elena Dubok,</p>
<p>    Ludmila Gurieva)			     1:32:17.1</p>
<p>7. Slovakia (Martina Schwarzbacherova, Anna Murinova, Marcela</p>
<p>    Pavkovcekova, Sona MIhokova)	     1:33:35.7</p>
<p>8. Belarus (Natalia Ryzhenkova, Natalia Permiakova, Svetlana</p>
<p>    Belan, Svetlana Paramigina)		1:33:40.1</p>
<p>9. USA (Ntala Skinner, Stacey Wooley, Debbie Nordyke, Kristi</p>
<p>    Viljanen Sabasteanski)		     1:33:45.5</p>
<p>10.Finland ( Katja Holanti, Mari Lampinen, Tiina Mikkola,</p>
<p>    Annukka Mallat)				1:33:54.8</p>
